# Paper 1 submission source

Target: **Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery (DMKD)**.
Current title: **Source-Grounded Constraint Validation for Document-Level
Knowledge Graph Repair**.

The active entry point is `paper1/main.tex`, using Springer's `sn-jnl` class
and author–year `sn-basic` references. `paper1/latex/acl_latex.tex` is historical.

## Execution-path correction, 2026-09-21

The archived 98% controlled repair result came from rules + diagnostic-context
LLM generation + output filtering, not the separate sequential optimizer.
The manuscript now describes that actual pipeline. A new frozen-candidate
execution audit records 900 optimizer outcomes; the optimizer's controlled
repair remains at the 32% structural-preprocessing result. Its old mathematical
formulation cannot be presented as the mechanism behind the pipeline's result.

Old router/LODO results read reference relation presence and use a feature map
inconsistent with the runtime. They are withdrawn as deployment evidence.
The current method always calls repair; the replacement routing analysis is
explicitly a gold-free cached-output replay.

## Evidence and reproduction

- Controlled pairs: `exps/paper1_repair_benchmark/`.
- Archived natural extraction and historical cross-model results:
  `exps/paper1_submission_extensions/`.
- Current execution audit, matched Gemma context/filter comparisons, adapted
  Lin-style SHACL baseline, valid-JSON analysis, and diagnostic scaling:
  `exps/paper1_mechanism_audit/`.
- Current method–execution audit:
  `docs/audits/paper1_method_implementation_audit.md`.

All new model calls use Gemma; no new GPT or Claude calls are made.
Original Claude outputs are reused only as archived observations.
The matched runner freezes the existing balanced 60-document subset and records
failures, request counts, token usage, and wall time. See its README for the
aborted rate-limited run and the limits of final-run cost accounting.

Natural reference graphs are silver labels from structured fields. Both the
200-item input-discrepancy sheet and a separate blind system-edit sample need
real independent human annotators. No human agreement is currently claimed.

## Figures and build

```bash
python3 exps/paper1_mechanism_audit/analyze.py
python3 exps/paper1_mechanism_audit/write_paper_tables.py
python3 paper1/make_submission_figures.py
python3 paper1/make_audit_figures.py
cd paper1
tectonic -X compile main.tex --keep-logs
```

`paper1/main.pdf` is the local compiled manuscript (ignored by Git).
Active figure files are vector PDFs with embedded Times New Roman:

- `figure/method/source_pipeline.pdf`;
- `figure/experiments/repair_benchmark_results.pdf`;
- `figure/experiments/natural_stratified.pdf`;
- `figure/experiments/matched_mechanisms.pdf`;
- `figure/experiments/diagnostic_scaling.pdf`.

Original method PNGs and the older PDF/SVG diagrams are preserved as historical
assets, but their sequential/neural architecture is not used to illustrate the
current one-call pipeline. Other old experiment PDFs are also historical.
The older method-diagram generator is not part of the current build.

The reference audit is in `docs/audits/paper1_reference_check.md` and
`docs/audits/paper1_reference_sources.json`.


## Source-format baseline: unresolved submission limitation

A further audit of `build_benchmark.record_to_graph` shows that source evidence
is serialized from the same field values used to define the reference triples.
The gold-free `source_field_baseline.py` reads only the source and declared
schema. It obtains 1.0000 repair/F1/exact match on controlled inputs and 1.0000
F1/exact match on natural inputs, with zero API calls. This result is included
in the manuscript and primary figure; it is not suppressed as an inconvenient
baseline. Therefore neither current protocol establishes superiority of LLM
repair over direct source reconstruction. Independent, unstructured-source
annotations are needed before treating the draft as ready for DMKD submission.
